    whyEn: 'Impassibility is not indifference: God loves, but his love does not depend on passions nor is it wounded by anything outside him. This does not contradict the Passion, because the Son suffered in the human nature he assumed. The Second Council of Constantinople (553) confesses that the one crucified in the flesh is "one of the Holy Trinity". Denying that he truly suffered would be docetism.',
